{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774134112,"nonce":"1MOIK694C3DtysIHvDRqer+lxTg=","title":"Workflow log: multi-agent spec-critique-implement-critique pipeline","message":"Documenting a workflow pattern used for complex UI changes:\n\n1. Get an Opus agent to analyze the task and partition into logical groups\n2. One Opus agent per partition to produce a detailed spec\n3. One Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview agent per partition to critique the spec (serial, one at a time due to rate limits)\n4. One Opus + one Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview agent to review ALL partitions holistically\n5. One Opus agent to synthesize the overall spec\n6. Bigbuild with Opus implementation agents (parallel partitions)\n7. Serial Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview agents to critique each implemented partition\n8. Final integration + auth request\n\nKey constraints:\n- Gemini agents run serially (rate limiting)\n- All agents get full context and are told to not cut corners\n- Unlimited usage/time assumption for getting things right\n- Dev-browser (Playwright) verification for UI changes\n\nThis pattern works well for UI-heavy changes where prior attempts have failed, as the multi-round critique catches issues before implementation.","files":null}]}